INT. SLEEPER TRAIN - COMPARTMENT - NIGHT

Two bunks, a fold-down table, a window streaked with rain. The train clatters through a tunnel. A lamp swings.

IGNATIUS FELLOWES (60s, silk dressing gown, nightcap) sits upright on the lower bunk with a book. PHILOMENA "PHIL" ACHTERBERG (30s, trench coat, boots still on) leans against the door. MORDECAI VANTONGEREN (40s, wire glasses, medical bag) stands by the window.

IGNATIUS
Phil, would you sit? You're making the lamp nervous.

PHIL
Ignatius, I'm not leaving the door.

MORDECAI
Phil, with respect, it's a train. The door isn't going anywhere.

PHIL
Neither are we.

The lamp flickers. Something knocks softly from the ceiling. All three look up.

IGNATIUS
Mordecai, did you hear that?

MORDECAI
I did. It's the luggage rack.

PHIL
It's not the luggage rack.

IGNATIUS
(muttering)
Third time since Prague.

MORDECAI
(to Ignatius)
Sir, you must rest.

IGNATIUS
(to the room)
I will rest when someone tells me what we shipped in the baggage car.

PHIL
(over him)
Nobody shipped anything.

MORDECAI
(over her)
The manifest says medical supplies.

IGNATIUS
Mordecai, you wrote the manifest!

MORDECAI
Ignatius, I wrote what I was told.

PHIL
By whom?

Three knocks, slow, from the ceiling. The train enters another tunnel. The lamp dies. In the dark, a fourth knock comes from inside the door, right beside Phil's ear.

PHIL (CONT'D)
(very quiet)
Don't anybody move.

IGNATIUS
(whisper)
Mordecai. Say something.

MORDECAI
(whisper)
Phil, if you'd open the door...

PHIL
Mordecai, no.

The knocking stops. The train bursts into moonlight. In the sudden pale glow they see the door handle slowly turning down.
